  "outlookText": "000\nACPN50 PHFO 051742\nTWOCP \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS Central Pacific Hurricane Center Honolulu HI\nIssued by NWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n800 AM HST Thu Nov 05 2026\n\nFor the central North Pacific...between 140W and 180W:\n\nEastern Central Pacific (CP95):\nShowers and thunderstorms associated with an area of low pressure\nlocated several hundred miles to the southeast of the Big Island of\nHawaii continue to become better organized. Environmental conditions\nare conducive for additional development, and a tropical depression\nis expected to develop, possibly as soon as later today. The system\nis forecast to move west-northwestward to westward at 10 to 15 mph,\npassing well south of the Hawaiian Islands.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...high...90 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...high...90 percent.\n\n$$\nForecaster Evans/Papin\nNNNN",
